            <ArticleTitle>Rapidly repeated intravenous boluses of salbutamol for acute severe asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>680-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the use of intravenous boluses of salbutamol given rapidly (over 1-2 min) in children (5 microg x kg-1) and young adults (250 microg) with acute severe asthma who were not improving with doses of nebulised salbutamol. Intravenous boluses were repeated within a short time until improvement was seen. Two of the seven patients required tracheal intubation and ventilation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
